Package: usual-install
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, flatpak, policykit-1 | polkitd
Recommends: chromium | chromium-browser | brave-browser | vivaldi-stable
Description: install applications from vendor download pages
 Usual Install makes a vendor's own "Download for Linux" button end in a
 working, installed application, the way an .exe installer does on Windows,
 instead of a tarball or an AppImage with no desktop entry.
 .
 A system service provisions every Chromium-family browser on the machine,
 including ones installed later, so there is no browser extension for the
 user to find or install. When a download page is recognised, the matching
 package is installed from Flathub or from the distribution's own
 repositories.
